# Read the rule before you finish

File-scoped rules are not in the prompt until a matching file is open. A new file is written before its rule attaches. Before editing, and again before you finish, read the rules below for the paths you changed.

`ProjectRuleIndexTest` fails the build when a file in `.cursor/rules/` is missing from this list.

## The build already checks

- `kotlin-detekt-ktlint-rpi-style.mdc`, `kotlin-magic-numbers-detekt.mdc`, `kotlin-detekt-top-level-property-naming.mdc`: `./gradlew :<module>:detekt` in CI.
- `composable-preview.mdc`: `ComposablePreviewRuleTest` in `:player:testDebugUnitTest`. A UI `@Composable` under `player/**/ui` needs a same-file `@Preview` that calls it. Each preview is private, `widthDp = 800` and `heightDp = 480` unless `name` is set, and wrapped in `RemoteScreensTheme`.
- `kotlin-core.mdc` (`GlobalScope`) and the no-XML-layout line in `jetpack-compose.mdc` and `android-architecture.mdc`: the same player test.
- `editor-preview-first-layout.mdc`: `editor/src/model/editorShell.test.ts` in `npm test`.
- `editor-naming-variables.mdc` and `vue3-composition-api-cursorrules-prompt-file.mdc`: `npm run lint` in CI.

## Read these for the files you touch

- Any `*.kt` or `*.kts`: `kotlin-core.mdc`, `kotlin-naming-variables.mdc`, and the three detekt rules above.
- `*Screen.kt`, `*Component.kt`, `*Composable.kt`, `ui/**/*.kt`: also `jetpack-compose.mdc` and `composable-preview.mdc`.
- `*ViewModel.kt`, `*Repository.kt`, `*Dao.kt`, `*Module.kt`, `di/**`, `data/**`: `android-architecture.mdc`.
- `editor/**`: `vue3-composition-api-cursorrules-prompt-file.mdc` and `editor-naming-variables.mdc`. The screen-editor shell also uses `editor-preview-first-layout.mdc`.

## Read the context rule when its files change

These describe behavior that is already shipped. Keep it when you edit those files.

- `mockup-ui-match-context.mdc` — player chrome and `GridMockup.vue`
- `theme-roles-editor-context.mdc` — theme roles
- `nav-icon-paint-context.mdc` — nav icon paint
- `session-document-rebuild-context.mdc` — document rebuild versus vars
- `map-dialog-player-osm-context.mdc` — map dialog
- `camera-dialog-live-video-context.mdc` — camera dialog
- `ha-weather-icons-context.mdc` — weather icons
- `standby-wake-sources-context.mdc` — wake sources
- `docs-wiki-screenshots-context.mdc` — docs, wiki, screenshots
- `freeform-text-style-controls-context.mdc` — free-form type
